# AGENTS.md

Conventions for coding agents working in {{.ProjectName}} ({{.AgentName}},
an agent-base downstream project).

## Commands

Operate this repo with agentctl; `./make.sh` is a thin shim over it.

| Task | Command |
| ---- | ------- |
| Ship the checked-out tree | `agentctl deploy` |
| Convergence check only | `agentctl deploy --dry-run` |
| Instance status | `agentctl status` |
| Instance logs | `agentctl logs` (`-f` to follow) |
| Pause / resume | `agentctl stop` / `agentctl start` |
| Tear down (volumes kept) | `agentctl destroy` (add `--volumes` to drop data) |
| Start the dev stack (overlay) | `agentctl dev up` |
| Stop the dev stack | `agentctl dev down` |
| Dev logs / restart | `agentctl dev logs -f` / `agentctl dev restart` |
| Update to the latest tree | `git pull --ff-only && agentctl deploy` |
| Validate spec + automations | `agentctl validate` |
| Secrets | `agentctl secrets {init\|check\|edit}` |
| Secrets alias | `agentctl env` |
| Worktree sharing agent/.env | `agentctl worktree {create\|remove} <branch>` |
| Open the gateway in a browser | `agentctl dev open` |
| Deployment platform | `agentctl platform {ls\|set\|check}` |
| Pre-flight report | `agentctl doctor` |
| Lint (pre-commit) | `agentctl check` |
| Install git hooks | `agentctl hooks` |
| Version | `agentctl version` |
| Shim for any command above | `./make.sh <command>` |

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| `agent/spec.json` | Declarative boot contract; the loader is fail-closed |
| `agent/Dockerfile` | Thin image over ghcr.io/tankdonut/agent-base |
| `agent/.env` | Secrets (gitignored); created from `agent/.env.example` |
| `agent/automations/` | Cron jobs as frontmatter-markdown files |
| `agent/workspace/` | Persona and memory seed content |
| `agent/skills/`, `knowledge/content/` | Skill and doc seed content |
| `compose.yml`, `compose.dev.yml` | Production service + dev overlay |
| `make.sh` | Thin shim delegating to agentctl |

## Key conventions

- The spec loader is fail-closed: an unknown key or unresolvable ref
  aborts the boot. Run `agentctl validate` after every `spec.json` edit.
- Secrets live only in `agent/.env` (gitignored) and `{env:NAME}` refs —
  never as literal values in `spec.json`, never committed, never logged.
- Automations are image-baked (`agent/automations/`), never bind-mounted:
  writable cron prompts would be an agent self-modification surface.
- Content under `agent/workspace/`, `agent/skills/`, and
  `knowledge/content/` seeds the data volume: workspace first boot, skills
  and docs replaced every boot — agent-authored files elsewhere on the
  volume survive.
